rock at McGulpin Point to measure the level of the water in Lake Michigan\n\t\t\t\t<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/2017-07-21-13.41.43.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"760\" height=\"428\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/2017-07-21-13.41.43.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/2017-07-21-13.41.43.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/2017-07-21-13.41.43-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/2017-07-21-13.41.43-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/2017-07-21-13.41.43-1024x576.jpg 1024w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 760px) 100vw, 760px\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div><\/figure><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/2017-07-21-14.31.43.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"760\" height=\"428\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/2017-07-21-14.31.43.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"\" aria-describedby=\"gallery-4-3984\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/2017-07-21-14.31.43.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/2017-07-21-14.31.43-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/2017-07-21-14.31.43-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/08\/2017-07-21-14.31.43-1024x576.jpg 1024w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 760px) 100vw, 760px\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<figcaption class='wp-caption-text gallery-caption' id='gallery-4-3984'>\n\t\t\t\tCrossing in the fog\n\t\t\t\t<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\n<p>We ended up the day heading on down I-75, then over to Kalkaska where my folks had lived in their retirement years and are buried at the Garfield Twp Cemetery. \u00a0Kathy and I drove around the area reminiscing how we used to come up here to see them when the kids were toddlers (they&#8217;re now 39 &amp; 40).<\/p>\n<p>All in all it was a great trip. \u00a0Seeing new sites along with revisiting some places we used to frequent and bringing back pleasant memories. \u00a0A great way to spend a few days in northern Michigan.<\/p>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>We left Charlevoix the next morning after a comfortable stay at the Maple Leaf Inn and continued north on M-31 toward Petoskey. \u00a0We had an opportunity to go along Lake Charlevoix on our way to Urgent Care (that&#8217;s another story altogether) when we happened along some of the famous &#8220;Mushroom Houses&#8221; we had heard about. &hellip; <a href=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/2017\/08\/09\/part-2-nwest-michigan-road-trip-mushrooms-tunnels-bears-and-indians-oh-my\/\" class=\"more-link\">Continue reading <span class=\"screen-reader-text\">Part 2 &#8211; N&#8217;West Michigan Road Trip &#8211; Mushrooms, Tunnels, Bears, and Indians &#8211; Oh My!<\/span><\/a><\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":4001,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"footnotes":""},"categories":[91,264,19546,554707329],"tags":[554707411,554707423,554707430,554707428,554707424,554707425,11110,554707422,554707426,554707427,554707429],"class_list":["post-3946","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","category-blogging","category-learning","category-sightseeing","category-traveling","tag-charlevoix","tag-cross-village","tag-kalkaska","tag-legs-inn","tag-m-22","tag-m-31","tag-michigan","tag-petoskey","tag-sand-dunes","tag-state-park","tag-village-bear"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.